      "writtenOn": "2026-03-13T16:13:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For C, the macros like ANDROID_KABI_RESERVED() are exclusively for use when merging LTS updates. They are not for new feature use. Is that what you intend here? If not, perhaps just `__reservedX` is a better name.\n\nCan you give an example of how these will look when one of them is used for something?",
      "revId": "4130616600153fe52c1798ad9c80f5eb7f514806",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5fba8dd6_3db4573a",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder/rust_binder_main.rs",
